501 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 166 0 R
/E (All communication with the Google Generative API is handled in this module. The module defaults to the gemini-3.5-flash model and falls back to a list of fallback models if the default is not available. A key design decision was to use the structured output mode where the API is instructed to respond with a JSON formatted response according to a predefined Pydantic schema, instead of freeform text. This makes the pipeline far more robust as there is no complex parsing of the output required.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
502 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 166 0 R
/E (If the book was under 350,000 characters, I just sent the entire text to the API in a single call. If it's a longer book, I adopted the map-reduce strategy: I split the text into chunks of up to 60,000 characters, summarized each chunk in parallel in individual calls, and then summarized the summaries. This gets around the token limit errors AND gives you the big picture.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
503 0 obj
<<
